an be determined', 0.9794416613476251], [[[178.0, 752.0], [1335.0, 752.0], [1335.0, 781.0], [178.0, 781.0]], "by measuring a patient's peripheral arterial oxygen saturation (SpO2). In acutely unwell patients", 0.9809400310221407], [[[174.0, 781.0], [1301.0, 782.0], [1301.0, 812.0], [174.0, 811.0]], 'it has been shown that giving a lower concentration of oxygen than usual, to achieve a lower', 0.990647352260092], [[[174.0, 843.0], [1317.0, 840.0], [1317.0, 876.0], [174.0, 879.0]], 'published following this suggests avoiding an SpO2 of >96% in these acutely unwell patients.4', 0.981584358279423], [[[174.0, 905.0], [1294.0, 906.0], [1294.0, 942.0], [174.0, 941.0]], 'therapy in patients receiving MV on an ICU,5-7 leaving a knowledge gap that requires urgent', 0.9858123751787039], [[[176.0, 973.0], [824.0, 972.0], [824.0, 1002.0], [176.0, 1003.0]], 'know the ideal SpO2 target for patients receiving MV.', 0.9871800182000646], [[[177.0, 1028.0], [589.0, 1029.0], [589.0, 1059.0], [177.0, 1058.0]], '1.2 Review of existing evidence', 0.9894616680760537], [[[176.0, 1095.0], [1312.0, 1097.0], [1312.0, 1126.0], [176.0, 1124.0]], 'For a number of years it has been suggested that excessive oxygen administration may harm', 0.9769917177350333], [[[179.0, 1128.0], [1193.0, 1128.0], [1193.0, 1157.0], [179.0, 1157.0]], 'critically ill patients.8 The majority of data in the intensive care literature comes from', 0.9646430171198315], [[[180.0, 1161.0], [1242.0, 1161.0], [1242.0, 1187.0], [180.0, 1187.0]], 'retrospectiveobservationalstudiesofexistingdatabasesandtheyprovidecontradictory', 0.9976617218572882], [[[174.0, 1186.0], [1313.0, 1186.0], [1313.0, 1222.0], [174.0, 1222.0]], 'findings.1. 9, 10 A substantial limitation to this approach is the assumption that survival might be', 0.9888977545499802], [[[178.0, 1285.0], [1305.0, 1284.0], [1305.0, 1314.0], [178.0, 1315.0]], 'oxygenated). The observational nature of these studies and small sampling window preclude', 0.9905142047432032], [[